        "timestamp": 1775998757,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Orban and Magyar face off in historic vote Europe Issued on: 12/04/2026 - 14:59 Hungarians are heading to the polls for a pivotal election in the country. Orban, 62, who is seeking a fifth straight term, has transformed his country into a model of illiberal democracy, following Trump in casting migration and \"woke\" values as a \"civilisational\" threat.Former government insider Magyar, 45, burst onto the scene just two years ago, amassing support against the backdrop of economic stagnation, despite an electoral system skewed in favour of Orban's Fidesz party. Senior fellow for Europe at the Council on Foreing Relations, Liana Fix, shares further insights. Orban's 16-year grip on power under threat from Magyar 12/04/2026 Europe Hungary: Centre-right Tisza party tipped to defeat Orban's Fidesz 12/04/2026 Europe Polls open in Hungary crunch vote 12/04/2026 Europe Hungary: Orban and Magyar on the home stretch 12/04/2026 Europe Among Magyar's supporters, \"one word keeps coming up: hope\" 12/04/2026 Europe 'Trump harbors an unexplained sympathy for Vladimir Putin', Ukrainian analyst says 10/04/2026 Europe Hungary: Is Viktor Orban Russia's 'Trojan horse' in the EU? 10/04/2026 Europe France plans 36 billion euro boost to rearmament, nuclear deterrent expansion 08/04/2026 Europe EU farm fraud scandal rocks Greek government, PM urges swift action 07/04/2026 Europe"
